that the stamps have been duly cancelled;
(6)
that on each paper the number and aggregate value of the stamps on it have been recorded;
(7)
that the rules made by the State Government for regulating the number of stamps to be used for denoting fees have
been complied with;
(8)
that there is nothing suspicious in the appearance of the stamps;
(9)
that all orders have been duly signed;
(10)
that all necessary receipts are in the record.

